{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"update.json\", \"summary\": \"Requested a suffrage variant for the VerifyLeader account, whose first limitation says only five members with two non-voters were exercised and that a single non-voter was untested. The harness bootstraps four voters, demotes one, waits until that member's own configuration no longer lists it as a voter, then cuts the leader from the two other voters: the trigger leaves the single non-voter reachable, the control cuts it as well. A local probe produced the same pair as the earlier shape, with verification succeeding immediately when the non-voter could answer and failing with a leadership-lost message once it was cut, which would generalise the defect to a three-voter cluster where the voter quorum is two and only the leader itself can answer for the voters. Two comparisons encode the required behaviour, that a verification succeed only when support the configuration counts is reachable, expecting the trigger to be violated and the control to hold; the prerequisites pin the membership counts, the reachable counts and the voter quorum so the receipt shows exactly which shape ran. The submission validates with zero schema errors, the harness file exists, and it requests one execution.\"}"}}
